<title>USA: Aeroquip-Vickers unit wins $70 mln contract.</title>
<headline>Aeroquip-Vickers unit wins $70 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>MAUMEE, Ohio 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aeroquip-Vickers Inc said its subsidiary has been awarded a $70 million contract by McDonnell Douglas Corp's military transport aircraft division to support the C-17 Globemaster III aircraft.</p>
<p>Under the contract, parts will be procured over the next seven years for production of 80 aircraft beginning in 1998.</p>
<p>This award is in addition to a contract worth about $40 million already won by the subsidiary, Vickers Inc, and its sister company, Aeroquip Corp, for the C-17.</p>
<p>(-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610)</p>
